# DAB Project — Rule Manifest

This is the primary entry point for AI agent rules in the DAB repository. Rules are organized into modular files; **Cursor loads** the copies in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`. The canonical editable sources remain in `.agents/rules/` (kept in sync by convention).

## Rule hierarchy

### 1. Global project rules

These apply to all packages and establish core architectural and behavioral standards.

- **Global**: `dab-global.mdc` (source: `.agents/rules/global.md`) — Clean Architecture, tech stack (Dart/Flutter), agent behavior.

### 2. Pattern rules

Detailed patterns when writing specific kinds of code (both packages).

- **Functional programming**: `dab-functional-programming.mdc` — `Either`, `fpdart`, `AppFailure`, `guardedCall`; never throw as control flow.
- **Data classes**: `dab-data-classes.mdc` — entities, `dart_mappable`, immutability, sealed classes, `build_runner`.
- **Views**: `dab-views.mdc` — view hierarchy, Riverpod notifiers/states, layouts, naming.
- **Extensions**: `dab-extensions.mdc` — naming and placement of Dart extensions.

### 3. Maintenance rules

Keep supporting artifacts in sync with code changes.

- **Documentation**: `dab-doc-maintenance.mdc` — updating `doc/*.md`.
- **Bruno**: `dab-bruno-maintenance.mdc` — updating the `bruno/` API collection.
- **Commits**: `dab-commit.mdc` (source: `.agents/rules/commit.md`) — commits only when the user explicitly asks; one commit per request; issue-key subjects when applicable; no AI/tool attribution in messages.
- **Project management**: `dab-project-manager.mdc` (source: `.agents/rules/project-manager.md`) — PO/PM boundaries, Linear ticket hygiene, and delivery gatekeeping.

### 4. Package-specific rules

- **DAB API**: `dab-api-package.mdc` (source: `dab_api/.agents/rules.md`) — Relic, Drift, server patterns.
- **DAB App**: `dab-app-package.mdc` (source: `dab_app/.agents/rules.md`) — Riverpod, go_router, ObjectBox, custom `ServiceLocator`.

### 5. Workflows (opt-in / manual)

- **Planning (`@plan`)**: `dab-plan.mdc`
- **Implementation (`@code`)**: `dab-code.mdc`
- **Scaffold view**: `dab-workflow-sc-view.mdc`

> **Tip:** Read **dab-global** first, then package supplements. If something conflicts, follow global rules and call out the deviation.
